    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d237">

                <pb facs="0319" n="203" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg203"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.51/1211.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Sullivan.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-30T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 30, 1914, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your January 28, 2 p.m., and January 29, 3 p.m. Since you state a month may
                    elapse pending approval by both Houses of Congress of plan suggested, immediate
                    relief will be supplied by having Bureau of Insular Affairs direct the General
                    Receiver of Dominican Customs to pay the Government five thousand dollars per
                    day, this amount not to be exceeded until the General Receiver has segregated
                    the amount which he is required to transmit to New York for the month of
                    February. Is Department correct in considering this amount sufficient to care
                    for temporary daily requirements?</p>
                <p>This Department does not look with favor upon the suggestion of the Banco
                    Nacional that it be provided with Dominican Government’s funds to lend to that
                    Government.</p>
                <p>Dominican Congress might recommend negotiating bonds so as to produce $1,650,000,
                    but this Department cannot undertake in advance to approve payments therefrom
                    except upon duly proved obligations in which claims for arms, ammunition or
                    supplies to revolutionists are not to be included.</p>
                <p>The title commercial attaché is accepted subject to understanding that
                    Government’s letter of request shall unmistakably embrace all the duties he is
                    to perform as indicated in Department’s January 26, 3 p.m.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
